<title>USA: U.S. Oct wholesale inventories rose 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct wholesale inventories rose 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department report of</p>
<p>wholesale inventories and sales, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p> (Percent Changes)     Oct   Sept--Rev from  Oct96/95</p>
<p> Inventories Total     0.6   -0.7    -1.3     1.6</p>
<p> Sales Total	     0.3    0.7     0.9     6.5</p>
<p> (Billions of dollars)    Oct   Sept--Rev from   Oct95</p>
<p> Inventories Total  258.61  256.96  255.52   254.56</p>
<p> -Durable Goods     163.73  163.92  163.24   160.88</p>
<p> --Cars/Parts	  27.86   27.24   26.86    27.29</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods  94.88   93.04   92.28    93.68</p>
<p> --Petroleum Prods.   5.52    5.10    5.10     4.82</p>
<p> (Billions of dollars)    Oct   Sept--Rev from   Oct95</p>
<p> Sales Total	  201.98  201.40  201.97   189.59</p>
<p> -Durable Goods     103.22  103.47  103.90    98.36</p>
<p> --Cars/Parts	  16.86   17.04   16.72    16.35</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods  98.77   97.93   98.08    91.23</p>
<p> --Petroleum Prods.  16.01   15.51   15.37    12.40</p>
<p>The October stock-to-sales ratio for merchant wholesalers, seasonally adjusted, was unchanged from September at 1.28 months' worth. September was previously reported at 1.27 months.</p>
<p>The ratio is a measure of how many months it would take to sell existing inventories at the current sales pace.</p>
</text>
